-- title:
--   Eigenform realising a Hecke maximal ideal congruent to a_ℓ(W)
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a Weierstrass curve over $\mathbb{Z}$, let $p$ and $N$ be natural numbers with $N \neq 0$, and let $S$ be a set of natural numbers. Write $\mathbb{T} =$ `heckeAlgebra N 2 S` for the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}}(S_2(\Gamma_0(N)))$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid N$ with $\ell \notin S$ together with the operators $U_q$ for primes $q \mid N$ with $q \notin S$. Let $\mathfrak{m} \subseteq \mathbb{T}$ be a maximal ideal containing the image of $p$, and assume that for every prime $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid N$ and $\ell \notin S$ one has $T_\ell - a_\ell(W) \in \mathfrak{m}$, where $a_\ell(W) = \#\mathbb{Z}/\ell + 1 - \#(W \bmod \ell)$ is the trace of Frobenius of the reduction of $W$ modulo $\ell$. Then there exist a cusp form $f$ of weight $2$ on $\Gamma_0(N)$ and an ideal $\mathfrak{m}'$ of the ring $\overline{\mathbb{Z}}$ of elements of $\mathbb{C}$ integral over $\mathbb{Z}$ such that: $f$ is a normalised eigenform in the sense that its $q$-expansion coefficients (of width $1$) satisfy $a_1(f) = 1$, $a_{mn}(f) = a_m(f)a_n(f)$ for coprime $m, n$, $a_{p^{r+2}}(f) = a_p(f)a_{p^{r+1}}(f) - p\,a_{p^r}(f)$ for primes $p \nmid N$, and $a_{p^{r+2}}(f) = a_p(f)a_{p^{r+1}}(f)$ for primes $p \mid N$; $\mathfrak{m}'$ is maximal and contains $p$; and for every prime $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid N$, $\ell \notin S$ there is an $a \in \overline{\mathbb{Z}}$ whose image in $\mathbb{C}$ is the $\ell$-th $q$-expansion coefficient of $f$ and which satisfies $a - a_\ell(W) \in \mathfrak{m}'$.
--
--   This is the passage, in the style of Deligne–Serre, from a maximal ideal of the weight-$2$ Hecke algebra carrying the Frobenius traces of an elliptic curve to an actual normalised eigenform whose coefficients are congruent to those traces modulo a maximal ideal of $\overline{\mathbb{Z}}$ above $p$. It is the exit step of the level-lowering chain, used by the statements producing a normalised eigenform of level dividing $N$ attached to the curve.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_WeierstrassCurve_exists_isNormalizedEigenform_and_qCoeff_sub_apOfModel_mem_of_ideal_heckeAlgebra.lean

